  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef wants to become fit for which he decided to walk to the office and return home by walking. It is known that Chef's office is XXX km away from his home.\n\nIf his office is open on 555 days in a week, find the number of kilometers Chef travels through office trips in a week.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nEach test case contains of a single line consisting of single integer XXX.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the number of kilometers Chef travels through office trips in a week.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤X≤101 \\leq X \\leq 101≤X≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1\n3\n7\n10",
        "output": "10\n30\n70\n100",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The office is 111 km away. Thus, to go to the office and come back home, Chef has to walk 222 kms in a day. In a week with 555 working days, Chef has to travel 2⋅5=102\\cdot 5 = 102⋅5=10 kms in total.\nTest case 222: The office is 333 kms away. Thus, to go to the office and come back home, Chef has to walk 666 kms in a day. In a week with 555 working days, Chef has to travel 6⋅5=306\\cdot 5 = 306⋅5=30 kms in total.\nTest case 333: The office is 777 kms away. Thus, to go to the office and come back home, Chef has to walk 141414 kms in a day. In a week with 555 working days, Chef has to travel 14⋅5=7014\\cdot 5 = 7014⋅5=70 kms in total.\nTest case 444: The office is 101010 kms away. Thus, to go to the office and come back home, Chef has to walk 202020 kms in a day. In a week with 555 working days, Chef has to travel 20⋅5=10020\\cdot 5 = 10020⋅5=100 kms in total."
      }
    ]
  },
